<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The Android adaptive-icon foreground: the Stash mark, as a vector.

    A vector rather than a bitmap because the launcher draws this at sizes from
    48dp to 192dp and a PNG only looks right at the density it was rendered for.
    The geometry is the same traced path as `public/icons/foreground.svg`,
    scaled into the 108-unit adaptive canvas.

    Android masks an adaptive icon to whatever shape the launcher uses, and the
    region guaranteed to survive every one of those shapes is a 66-unit circle
    centred on the 108-unit canvas. At `0.145` the mark's box is 37.5 by 49.7
    units, a half-diagonal of 31.1 against a safe radius of 33, so no mask clips
    it, and the mark occupies 46% of the canvas, which is the proportion Google's
    own adaptive icons use.

    The mark is two pieces: a kept ribbon whose fold is the letter S, with the S
    cut between them. The colour is the icon's white; the tile behind it is the
    ink background layer. The icon is the one surface that is the same in light
    and dark mode, so neither value changes between the day and night resource
    sets.

    Note for editors: this is an XML comment, so a doubled hyphen cannot appear
    inside it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
